\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8.12}{\ignorespaces Heap allocation over the default scope of 463 patterns and 11\,395 entries. \emph  {Total allocated} counts every allocation, including memory later freed, and measures allocator pressure. \emph  {Max live peak} is the highest live-byte high-water mark within a single call and measures the footprint a deployment would see. The two are different quantities: total is cumulative and can exceed the live peak, because freed memory is counted in the former but not the latter. Timed-out entries are excluded from both, so both are lower bounds on the standard variants' true footprint.}}{81}{table.caption.63}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:memory}{{8.12}{81}{Heap allocation over the default scope of 463 patterns and 11\,395 entries. \emph {Total allocated} counts every allocation, including memory later freed, and measures allocator pressure. \emph {Max live peak} is the highest live-byte high-water mark within a single call and measures the footprint a deployment would see. The two are different quantities: total is cumulative and can exceed the live peak, because freed memory is counted in the former but not the latter. Timed-out entries are excluded from both, so both are lower bounds on the standard variants' true footprint}{table.caption.63}{}}
